[Music]  hi  i'm kit ong i'm a spatial designer  that's my main profession but i also do  multi-disciplinary  design as well and i collaborated in a  lot of other  cross-disciplinary projects my design  philosophy is  art of imperfection perfection of design  this is arise from my love for natural  material or the usage of natural  material like timber  natural stones and so on in most of my  projects  and the perfection of design is because  we are  very meticulous when it comes to detail  so  for example in a special project we  would go down to the very last boat  as a designer in the build industry  sometimes we do need to  hunt for small accessories as well as  the different assortment of furnitures  and in fact tambunya building is one of  the places that we usually go to  and don't be deceived by the plain  looking building inside is an enclave of  big and small furniture companies that  sells  an area of all different types of  furniture locally made as well as  internationally imported this is a  treasure  cove for anyone not just designers  homeowners alike to look for  unique pieces of furniture as well as  accessories  the interesting part of this is that  this warehouse look alike shops  in fact are properly done up showrooms  as well so a lot of customers are able  to  actually get some kind of ideas and  mock-up by  visiting the different pockets of the  buildings  [Music]  many of singaporeans now like to dine at  the air-conditioned food courts  and even in restaurants but i think  the hawker centers are one of the charm  of singapore  food scene and one of the better design  hawker centers is in fact very near to  my home which is a rangoon garden market  and food center  so this place is well designed with a  central courtyard that allows the whole  space to be well ventilated for an unair  conditioned area  it's very airy and very comfortable to  die in and  not forgetting there are many of my  favorite foods there  this is my home at hillside since the  new normal i've started  to juggle between working from home and  from the office  in fact the house was designed as a open  concept spaces so in a sense there are  ample spaces for us to maneuver around  and to  still create that virtual individual  spaces  first thing we did is to tear down the  wall of the  very narrow terrace house so after the  war was torn down we replaced it with  giant glass doors so these are pivot  doors that can be opened fully so in the  way we  actually created a much bigger livable  space  and at the same time we also turn the  car garage  into a patio so that extended the  outdoor space  to the living spaces after a hard day's  work usually i like to hang around with  friends you know sign up for drinks or  coffee  you know and holland is one of the very  nice enclaves  what attracts me to this place is in  fact the uh eclectic  mix of new shop fronts that will pop up  every now and then  when i visited you know and one of the  favorite place in holland view that i  usually visit is a 2am desert bar  i think the unique part about 2m is that  the chef janice wong even took the  effort to redesign some of the  tablewares  to present her dessert in a unique style  and as well as to redesign  some of the papers and chairs to allow  a communal dine-in for dessert  cross-collaboration works both ways we  are all putting our  best part of our profession on the table  you know so that everyone share  knowledges  and we will cross path at some point you  know  creating new sparks for a new product  so be it whether it's spatial design or  product design  or in fact any form of design you know  so that is just a medium that we express  our  creativity in a collective manner one of  the greatest passion in life that i have  is my love for  riding so i've been riding for the past  20 years in fact  on two wheels you feel alive when the  winds are blowing against your face and  that's where you can forget  a lot of things you know and sometimes  even recompose  about a certain problem so usually late  at night sometimes just like to take the  bite out for a spin  as a designer this profession is not an  easy path  but somehow i think that one word  passion  is the one that keeps us alive that  allows us to continue to persevere  in what we like to do what we love to do  in fact this is the only viewer  that kept us going continue to be  passionate in what you are doing  i think it can move mountains  you

